{"title":"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, the large rectangle is divided into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> smaller rectangles.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/a/cea41e3c382f23a81801dea51a23b1514ae6351f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] usepackage(&quot;mathptmx&quot;); // Times New Roman font defaultpen(miterjoin); unitsize(0.4cm);  // Parameters real grayBoxWidth = 1.8; real whiteBoxSpacing = 3.4; real height = 6.6 * grayBoxWidth; int nBoxes = 5;  real labelOffset = 1.3; real veryThickWidth = 1.0pt; real fontSize = 10pt;  pen grayFill = rgb(0.6, 0.6, 0.6); // hex #999999 pen veryThick = black + linewidth(veryThickWidth);  defaultpen(fontsize(fontSize));  pair[] Pb = new pair[5]; pair[] Pt = new pair[5];  for (int i = 0; i &lt; 5; ++i) {   real xPos = (grayBoxWidth + whiteBoxSpacing) * i;   Pb[i] = (xPos, 0);   Pt[i] = (xPos + grayBoxWidth, height);   filldraw(box(Pb[i], Pt[i]), grayFill, veryThick); }  // Outer rectangle draw(box(Pb[0], Pt[4]), veryThick);  // Label $w$ real yDim = height + labelOffset; real xMax = Pt[4].x; path labelLine = (0, yDim) -- (xMax, yDim); draw(labelLine, veryThick, Bars(6pt));  // Label w with white fill label(Label(&quot;$w$&quot;), (xMax / 2, yDim), fontsize(14pt), Fill(white)); [/asy]\" width=\"432\" height=\"258\" />\n</p><p>Each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> smaller shaded rectangles has a width of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> smaller unshaded rectangles has a width of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The width, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />, of the larger rectangle is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/3/383404e54ada883fb4b540515683a76389448bd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 20 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 32 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 52 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 56 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 68$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We see that the smaller shaded rectangles contribute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/c/49c5626e8e4ea770014a1bfcb31b3d66e01e8fb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\times 4 = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> units to the width and that the smaller unshaded rectangles contribute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/b/75b8dd4a36d5d53fb2c39a5413048e62a6e5db90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\times 8 = 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> units to the width from the information given in the problem and the diagram.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/d/73dc0eb522adf235a32513b654ff1653649b7ef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w = 20 + 32 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 52}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"187\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley\">2025 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problem